{"id": "2026-11-01-news-riots-follow-youth-demos-in-zurich-and-basel", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Riots follow youth demos in Zurich and Basel", "summary": "Unauthorised demonstrations in Zurich and Basel on 31 October ended in rioting, with burning barricades, a torched car and police using water cannon and rubber bullets.", "url": "https://www.polizei.bs.ch/medienmitteilungen/jsd/2026-unbewilligte-demonstration-behindert-den-verkehr-der-innenstadt", "source_domain": "polizei.bs.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Unauthorised demonstrations in Zurich and Basel on the night of Saturday 31 October ended in rioting, with barricades set on fire in both cities. In Zurich, several hundred people, some in Halloween masks, gathered on the Langstrasse at about 22:30 under the slogan «On en a marre – en Suisse aussi» (\"We've had enough – in Switzerland too\"), an echo of the youth protests in France and Germany. City police said a \"violent mob\" attacked officers with fireworks, stones and bottles, and police answered with a water cannon, irritant gas and rubber bullets. A car was set alight, and shop windows and the Stauffacher tram stop were smashed. Police also said a crowd attacked a patrol called to help a teenager badly hurt in an accident, forcing the officers to pull back before they could reach him. Zurich cantonal police arrested two young men carrying sand-weighted gloves, which count as weapons, and face coverings. According to the police, left-wing extremist groups had called the Zurich march. In Basel, cantonal police said about 150 people marched through the city centre without a permit, public transport had to be halted, and protesters built and burned barricades on St. Johanns-Platz.", "why": "this is the first time the protest wave sweeping France and Germany has led to violence in Swiss cities. It came two days after the arson attack in Thun (below), which a claim video also ties to the same movement.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-riots-follow-youth-demos-in-zurich-and-basel", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Zurich", "Basel", "Stadtpolizei Zürich"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-video-ties-thun-arms-plant-fire-to-protests", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Video ties Thun arms-plant fire to protests", "summary": "A claim video links the arson that destroyed the Thun headquarters of rubber-bullet launcher maker B&T to the European youth protests; Bern police are checking it.", "url": "https://www.nzz.ch/schweiz/brand-der-waffenfabrik-in-thun-war-ein-racheakt-der-linksextremen-ld.10050909", "source_domain": "nzz.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A claim-of-responsibility video ties the fire that destroyed the Thun headquarters of arms maker Brügger & Thomet (B&T) on the night of Wednesday 28 to Thursday 29 October to the European youth protests, NZZ reported on Sunday 1 November. Bern police treat the fire as arson. Nobody was hurt, and the damage is put at 12 to 20 million francs. B&T makes the GL06 launcher for \"less-lethal\" rubber projectiles, sold in France as the LBD 40. Rubber projectiles regularly cause serious injuries, and at least eight protesters are reported to have lost an eye in the recent French protests. The video, which circulated in France and Switzerland, shows incendiary devices being set off inside the building and the message \"Swiss, France, Germany, in the street with Gen Z\". Bern cantonal police are checking whether the video is authentic and have not named any suspects. Owner Karl Brügger told Blick that French police use ammunition from French maker Alsetex, not B&T's.", "why": "if the video is genuine, it would be an act of political sabotage on Swiss soil linked to the protest wave, aimed at a Swiss arms exporter.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-video-ties-thun-arms-plant-fire-to-protests", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Brügger & Thomet", "Thun", "Kantonspolizei Bern"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-greens-leader-balks-at-svp-s-amaudruz", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Greens leader balks at SVP's Amaudruz", "summary": "Greens president Lisa Mazzone criticised SVP Federal Council hopeful Céline Amaudruz over her ties to private bank Reyl ahead of the 9 December election.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/nachfolge-parmelin-gruenen-praesidentin-hat-grosse-probleme-mit-celine-amaudruz", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Greens president Lisa Mazzone said on Saturday 31 October that SVP Federal Council candidate Céline Amaudruz's ties to the Geneva private bank Reyl are \"a very big problem\" for her. Speaking on SRF's Samstagsrundschau, Mazzone pointed to Amaudruz's \"strong lobbying\" for a bank that \"long did business with Russia\". Amaudruz, the only woman among the SVP hopefuls, worked for Reyl until the end of September. Media have reported that the financial regulator FINMA criticised Reyl for weak anti-money-laundering safeguards, and that Amaudruz then filed several motions in parliament criticising FINMA. The Greens will still invite the SVP candidates to a hearing, a change from past practice, but Mazzone doubts the group will recommend any of them. The Greens hold 23 of the Federal Assembly's 246 votes and will not field a candidate of their own against the SVP. The SVP group picks its ticket on Friday 20 November, and the Federal Assembly elects Guy Parmelin's successor on Wednesday 9 December.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-greens-leader-balks-at-svp-s-amaudruz", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lisa Mazzone", "Céline Amaudruz", "SVP", "Reyl"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-trump-names-iranian-site-he-wants-to-hit", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump names Iranian site he wants to hit", "summary": "Trump said the US still had to deal with one or two Iranian sites including Kuh-e Kolang near Natanz; Khamenei threatened an unlimited response and a Qatari LNG carrier was hit in the Gulf.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/11/01/donald-trump-menace-l-iran-de-nouvelles-frappes-sur-un-ou-deux-sites-dont-le-mont-kolang-pres-du-complexe-nucleaire-de-natanz_6804009_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Donald Trump said on Saturday 31 October that the US still has to \"take care of\" one or two Iranian sites, naming the Kuh-e Kolang tunnel complex near the Natanz nuclear site, and claimed this could be done \"in ten minutes\". Trump told reporters at Mar-a-Lago that he was \"in no hurry\" with Iran. Earlier the same day, Secretary of State Marco Rubio said at the G20 in Atlanta that Trump had made \"no decision\" and prefers a \"diplomatic solution\". Press reports cited by Le Monde point to a possible short, intense campaign after the US midterm elections on Tuesday 3 November. Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei warned in a written statement of a response that would be \"immediate, powerful and without geographical limit\" if Iran is attacked again, and told commanders to update their target lists. At sea, the Qatar Gas Transport Company said on Sunday that its liquefied natural gas (LNG) carrier Al Mayeda was hit by \"unidentified objects\" in the Gulf on Friday evening, 30 October, with no injuries and the ship still operational. Al Jazeera, citing International Maritime Organization and UKMTO data, says at least 29 ships were hit in October, the worst month since the US-Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February.", "why": "Trump has repeatedly announced endpoints to this war that did not hold, so his \"ten minutes\" claim is a statement of intent, not a plan. Naming a target in public while his own secretary of state says nothing is decided leaves the risk of new strikes after the midterms open, as the Gulf shipping crisis keeps getting worse.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-trump-names-iranian-site-he-wants-to-hit", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "Donald Trump", "Kuh-e Kolang", "Mojtaba Khamenei", "Qatar"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-germany-s-gen-z-protests-end-in-looting", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Germany's Gen Z protests end in looting", "summary": "Tens of thousands joined youth protests across Germany on 31 October; rioting and looting broke out on Frankfurt's Zeil and clashes near Cologne Cathedral.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Youth protests across Germany on Saturday 31 October drew tens of thousands of people and were mostly peaceful by day, but rioting and looting broke out in Frankfurt and clashes in Cologne that evening. The nationwide \"Gen Z regelt\" (\"Gen Z takes charge\") marches called for better schools, relief from rising living costs and more social justice. In Frankfurt, police sealed off the Zeil, one of Germany's busiest shopping streets, after rioters smashed windows, looted shops (including a gun shop) and attacked officers with incendiary devices. Hesse's interior minister said he suspects about 100 left-wing extremists started the violence. In Cologne, about 200 people threw bottles and bicycles at police outside the cathedral, and there were also disturbances in Hamburg, Bremen and Berlin. Organisers have called for new protests.", "why": "the movement began with French school students and has now spread to Germany and, on the same night, to Zurich and Basel. Night-time violence is now coming with every round of protests, and German politicians are blaming left-wing activists for it.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-germany-s-gen-z-protests-end-in-looting", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Germany", "Frankfurt", "Cologne"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-france-protests-shrink-to-320-000", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "France protests shrink to 320,000", "summary": "France's interior ministry counted 320,000 protesters on 31 October, with clashes in several cities and more than 290 arrests.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/more-than-290-arrested-in-france-as-some-weekend-protests-turn-violent/a-79818138", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "France's interior ministry counted 320,000 protesters nationwide on Saturday 31 October, 70,000 of them in Paris, and police made more than 290 arrests as some marches turned violent. The ministry said the declared marches went \"smoothly\", but that \"radical elements\" tried to reach city centres in Bordeaux, Toulouse and Marseille to vandalise and loot. Police fired tear gas in Paris and Lyon in the late afternoon, fires burned in Marseille, and there were clashes in Rennes and Toulouse. About 70,000 police and other security staff were on duty, march routes were moved away from city centres, and several cities imposed curfews, some of them aimed at minors. The protests started weeks ago over understaffed schools and have widened since mid-October to the cost of living. Unions, student groups and the Yellow Vest movement called Saturday's marches, and more school blockades are planned.", "why": "the turnout was well below the 550,000 the ministry counted on Saturday 17 October, and arrests were far fewer than the 1,800 made that day. The movement is shrinking but has not stopped.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-france-protests-shrink-to-320-000", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Laurent Nuñez", "Yellow Vests"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-brussels-backs-tusk-in-polish-court-fight", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Brussels backs Tusk in Polish court fight", "summary": "The European Commission said appointing eight new Constitutional Tribunal judges is the Sejm's competence, urging President Nawrocki to validate them.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/10/31/crise-politique-en-pologne-bruxelles-appelle-le-president-karol-nawrocki-a-valider-la-nomination-de-nouveaux-juges-au-tribunal-constitutionnel_6803801_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The European Commission sided with Prime Minister Donald Tusk in Poland's constitutional-court standoff on Saturday 31 October, saying that appointing eight new judges to the Constitutional Tribunal is the job of the Sejm (the lower house). President Karol Nawrocki has refused to swear in the Sejm's picks. A Commission spokesperson told AFP that Polish authorities must make sure the tribunal works in line with Poland's constitution and the case law of the EU Court of Justice. Nawrocki held talks with the governing coalition and the opposition Law and Justice (PiS) party on Saturday without result. Judge Anna Korwin-Piotrowska, appointed under the current majority, was still at the tribunal claiming to be acting president, a day after riot police secured the building and the justice minister asked for the PiS-appointed tribunal president's immunity to be lifted. Tusk said in a video on Saturday evening that \"a democratic state must be strong\", but offered no way out of the deadlock.", "why": "Brussels taking a side gives Tusk political cover, but it does not solve the legal problem. Poland now has two rival claims to lead its top court a little over a year before a general election.", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-brussels-backs-tusk-in-polish-court-fight", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Poland", "European Commission", "Donald Tusk", "Karol Nawrocki", "Constitutional Tribunal"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-un-staffer-dies-in-houthi-detention", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "UN staffer dies in Houthi detention", "summary": "UN rights chief Volker Türk demanded an independent probe into the death of Mohammad el Shami, a UN human rights office staffer held by the Houthis since June 2024.", "url": "https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168716", "source_domain": "news.un.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "UN human rights chief Volker Türk on Saturday 31 October demanded an independent investigation into the death of Mohammad el Shami, a Yemeni staff member of his office who had been held by the Houthis since 6 June 2024. His family says he died more than a month ago but was told only recently, and has been given no explanation of how he died. Türk called on the Houthi authorities to hand over all medical and detention records and preserve evidence. El Shami was one of 13 UN staff seized in raids in June 2024. As of mid-October, the UN says 71 of its personnel are held by the Houthis, seven of them from Türk's office, and the Secretary-General's office said in June that another UN colleague had already died in detention.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-un-staffer-dies-in-houthi-detention", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Houthis", "Yemen", "Volker Türk", "OHCHR"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-venezuela-reportedly-bombs-eln-camp", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "Venezuela reportedly bombs ELN camp", "summary": "An NGO says a bombing attributed to Venezuela's army killed several ELN guerrillas at a camp in Apure state near the Colombian border on 30 October.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/am%C3%A9riques/20261101-plusieurs-morts-dans-le-bombardement-d-un-camp-de-la-gu%C3%A9rilla-colombienne-au-venezuela", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A bombing attributed to Venezuela's army killed several members of the Colombian ELN guerrilla group at a camp in Apure state, near the Colombian border, on Friday 30 October, the Venezuelan NGO Fundaredes told AFP. The NGO's director, Javier Tarazona, said a staff member counted nine bodies near Buena Vista del Meta. Fundaredes shared a video showing bodies, felled trees and a destroyed camp, and called it Venezuela's \"first bombing against the ELN\", which has been the strongest active guerrilla group in Latin America since most of the FARC disarmed in 2016. Venezuelan authorities did not respond to AFP.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-venezuela-reportedly-bombs-eln-camp", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-10-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Venezuela", "ELN", "Colombia", "Fundaredes"]}
{"id": "2026-11-01-news-eu-adds-2-fee-on-small-foreign-parcels", "date": "2026-11-01", "stream": "news", "headline": "EU adds €2 fee on small foreign parcels", "summary": "From 1 November the EU charges a €2 handling fee on small parcels from outside the bloc, on top of the €3 duty introduced in July.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/europe/20261101-ue-une-nouvelle-taxe-sur-les-petits-colis-%C3%A9trangers-entre-en-vigueur-la-fast-fashion-chinoise-vis%C3%A9e", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A €2 handling fee on small parcels entering the EU from outside the bloc took effect on Sunday 1 November. It comes on top of the €3 customs duty on parcels worth up to €150 that began in July. Belgium's customs spokesperson said the money will pay for checks, since nearly 5.9 billion small parcels entered the EU in 2025. RFI reports that inbound small-parcel volumes have fallen 65% since the €3 duty started, and that the duty has raised €364 million. Chinese platforms such as Shein and Temu are the main target.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-01-news-eu-adds-2-fee-on-small-foreign-parcels", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-01", "event_date": "2026-11-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["European Union", "Shein", "Temu"]}
